      "writtenOn": "2025-11-10T22:05:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It should be, the rule from the .gni is `(is_win \u0026\u0026 !dawn_is_winuwp) || (is_linux \u0026\u0026 !is_chromeos) || is_mac`\n\nThe `is_XXX` vars are set from `target_os`, and specifically `is_wasm` is for `target_os \u003d \"emscripten\"`. Desktop Linux is `linux`, etc.\n\nSo as written this value should only ever be true if we are building for non-UWP windows, desktop linux or desktop mac. (android, cros, etc have their own target_os strings other than \u0027linux\u0027 to differentiate them from desktop linux)",
      "parentUuid": "549c135a_9e077384",
